# The repo root ignores *.pdf so that sample documents dropped in a working tree
# never get committed by accident. The golden fixture is the deliberate
# exception: it IS the test input, it is 1.8 KB, and it is regenerated
# byte-for-byte by ../make_fixture_pdf.py. Un-ignore it here rather than
# weakening the root rule.
!golden.pdf
# alpha.pdf is the second deliberate exception. golden.pdf renders fully opaque,
# so the comparator's premultiplied-alpha and transparent-halo detectors cannot
# fire on it; this one has a transparent page background, constant-alpha
# graphics states and an SMask cut-out image, which is what makes those two
# detectors live. Same provenance: hand-assembled by ../make_fixture_pdf.py.
!alpha.pdf
# outline.pdf is the third deliberate exception. No committed fixture had a
# document OUTLINE, and neither does the NASA scan the port has been screenshot
# against -- so the sidebar's Chapters list had nothing real to show and its
# nesting, its UTF-8 titles and its unresolved-destination case were untestable.
# This one carries a 6-entry two-level outline including an accented and a CJK
# title, which is exactly what a narrow CP1252 conversion mangles silently on
# this machine. 6.4 KB, same provenance: regenerated byte-for-byte by
# ../make_outline_fixture.py.
!outline.pdf
# selection.pdf is the fourth deliberate exception. No committed fixture had
# selectable NON-ASCII PAGE TEXT (outline.pdf's accented and CJK strings are
# outline titles -- metadata, not content) and none had a LINK ANNOTATION at
# all, so text selection, copy and link hit-testing had nothing real to run
# against. This one carries an ASCII line, an accented WinAnsi line, a CJK line
# through a glyphless Type3 font with a ToUnicode CMap (the same trick
# portable/core/tests/SPDFCoreCJKSelectionTests.c uses, and the exact shape of
# an OCR text layer), one internal /GoTo link to page 3 and one external /URI
# link. 2.6 KB, same provenance: regenerated byte-for-byte by
# ../make_selection_fixture.py.
!selection.pdf
# link_dest.pdf is the fifth deliberate exception. selection.pdf's one internal
# link points at the LAST of three pages, where every scroll clamps at the
# document's end -- so "landed on the destination's own y" and "landed on the
# target page's top" are the SAME NUMBER there, and the divergence the links
# track had to close could not be observed at all. This one is eight pages with
# four links chosen so that all four cases separate: a NAMED destination
# (resolvable through both /Dests and /Names /Dests, as a real authoring tool
# writes it) 232 pt down page 4, a direct array destination 642 pt down page 6,
# a /Fit destination carrying no point at all on page 8, and an external /URI.
# 17 KB, same provenance: regenerated byte-for-byte by
# ../make_link_dest_fixture.py.
!link_dest.pdf
